  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Murphy comes for an adult preventive visit, booked at his twelve-week review four weeks ago. The cold he had three weeks ago cleared within about ten days without antibiotics; he used no sedating cold products or decongestants, and his sleep returned to its recent pattern: asleep within about 20 minutes, about seven hours a night, and nightmares less than once a week. Since finishing Cognitive Processing Therapy he has kept up the worksheets and has not needed a booster session. He has had no thoughts of suicide or self-harm and keeps his safety plan. He completed the health risk assessment before the visit and has no new concerns. No lipid, glucose, HIV, hepatitis B, or hepatitis C test is on record. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Adult preventive visit, age 40, established patient</td></tr><tr><td>Recent illness</td><td>Common cold three weeks ago, resolved</td></tr><tr><td>Behavioral health</td><td>PTSD much improved after nine therapy sessions; no suicidal thoughts; safety plan kept</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>None; no over-the-counter medicines or supplements</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Post-traumatic stress disorder and chronic insomnia, both improved</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Independent; working full time</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good, and better than in the summer</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Close family and veteran peer connections; finds his work purposeful; stress manageable</td></tr><tr><td>Behavioral</td><td>Never smoker; no alcohol (AUDIT-C 0); no cannabis or other drugs; coffee in the morning only; walks or exercises three or four times a week; eats out several times a week</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About seven hours a night with the sleep routine; nightmares less than once a week</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Instrumental activities of daily living</td><td>Independent; manages his own work, money, and appointments</td></tr><tr><td>Home and personal safety</td><td>Smoke detectors working; wears a seat belt; the safety plan and lethal-means steps from intake remain in place</td></tr><tr><td>Vision, hearing, and dental</td><td>No vision or hearing concerns; sees a dentist yearly</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

