    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Adult preventive visit, age 40</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. Depression (PHQ-9 3), alcohol (AUDIT-C 0), drug use, and tobacco screens are negative. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Post-traumatic stress disorder, much improved (F43.10)</content>. Sustained recovery after nine Cognitive Processing Therapy sessions: PCL-5 24 at the September review and PHQ-9 3 today. No suicidal ideation since intake, and acute risk remains low. [S]<list><item>Continue the therapy skills and the safety plan.</item><item>PTSD and insomnia review with the PCL-5 and PHQ-9 at the three-month review planned in September.</item><item>Booster session with Dr. Lee if symptoms return.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Chronic insomnia, improved (G47.00)</content>. About seven hours a night, back to his recent pattern after the cold, without medication. [S]<list><item>Continue the sleep routine; cognitive behavioral therapy for insomnia if the insomnia returns.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Blood pressure in the elevated range</content>. Office readings since June have ranged from 124 to 132 mmHg systolic and 78 to 84 mmHg diastolic, 124/78 mmHg today. No diagnosis of hypertension is made from office readings alone. [S]<list><item>Home blood pressure readings twice a day for one week before the three-month review.</item><item>Fasting lipid panel and HbA1c ordered for cardiovascular risk estimation.</item><item>Diet and activity counseling given.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Overweight, BMI 27.0</content>. Weight down 1.3 kg since June. [S]<list><item>Aim for at least 150 minutes a week of moderate activity, fewer restaurant meals, and less salt.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 score 3; already followed in his PTSD care</td></tr><tr><td>Suicide risk</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No ideation since intake; the safety plan from intake was reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy drug use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No cannabis or other drug use</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never smoker; no nicotine products</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>124/78 mmHg; office readings in the elevated range since June, so a week of home readings is planned before the next review</td></tr><tr><td>Prediabetes and type 2 diabetes screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Age 35 to 70 with a BMI of 27.0; HbA1c ordered</td></tr><tr><td>Lipid screening and statin assessment</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Age 40; fasting lipid panel ordered to estimate ten-year cardiovascular risk</td></tr><tr><td>Healthy diet and physical activity counseling</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Brief counseling for elevated blood pressure readings and a BMI of 27.0</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time antigen and antibody test, with his consent; no prior result on record</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time antibody test with reflex RNA, with his consent</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time triple panel (surface antigen, surface antibody, and core antibody)</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>This season&apos;s vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>No record of a prior series; recommended for adults through 59; to start once the screening panel is back</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Discussed; he plans to get this season&apos;s vaccine at his pharmacy</td></tr><tr><td>Tdap</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Given about five and a half years ago; next booster due in about four and a half years</td></tr><tr><td>HPV vaccine</td><td>Declined</td><td>Shared decision for adults 27 to 45; after discussion he declined</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Starts at 45</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Shared decision-making starts at 55</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer and abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoker</td></tr><tr><td>Zoster vaccine</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Starts at 50</td></tr><tr><td>Anxiety screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Already under care for post-traumatic stress disorder</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 1964-1965 season [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Fasting lipid panel, HbA1c, and HIV, hepatitis C, and hepatitis B screening ordered; results will be sent when available. Hepatitis B vaccination once the screening result is back. One week of home blood pressure readings before the PTSD and insomnia review in about two months. Next preventive visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
